WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.760
It was a win that unified a divided country

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.440
We were united as a rainbow nation

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:17.120
In 1995, one year after the country’s first ever multi-racial elections...

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.200
...South Africa hosted—and won—the Rugby World Cup

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.760
When the final whistle went and I looked around the stadium...

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.280
...all different creeds and colour of people, they were hugging each other

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.600
It adds impetus to our nation-building effort

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.240
But 25 years later...

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.920
...South African rugby is still embroiled in the politics of race

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.320
Politics can never be separated from sport

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:52.520
I think we are more divided at this stage than we were then

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.440
Almost 90% of South Africans are black or mixed-race...

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.560
...yet they remain the minority in the Springboks, the national rugby team

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.000
In an attempt to get more black players into the top tier of the game...

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.640
...South Africa’s government introduced quotas...

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.240
...to force coaches to pick black players

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.160
But it’s a controversial strategy

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.080
Chester Williams was one of the first black players...

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.440
...to ever represent the Springboks

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.920
Definitely, quota means to me opportunity

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.280
Peter de Villiers was South Africa’s first black coach

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.800
I don’t think quotas is your solution

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.480
Both grew up in the black township of Paarl...

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.960
...but they feel very differently about quotas

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.720
Historically rugby is supposed to be played only by white people

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.720
Because of apartheid only the white people are selected for the Springbok team

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.360
I always wanted to be a Springbok myself

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.440
Chester Williams was the only black player...

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.200
...in the famous Mandela 1995 World Cup winning side

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.720
He inspired millions of South Africans

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.600
All I wanted was that opportunity so I can prove to the world...

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.520
...that black people can also play rugby

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.320
I represent not only myself but I represent...

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.160
...my community, I represent black people in South Africa

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.440
After retiring in 2000...

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.720
...Chester became a coach at the University of Western Cape

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.080
Being a so-called black or coloured player in South Africa...

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.560
...was challenging at times

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.600
I remember vividly they stopped me from going to have dinner...

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.840
...because I was the only black guy in the team...

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.840
...and at that time we were not allowed to dine with the white people

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.640
Securing a spot on the Springboks side wasn’t easy

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.480
You had to train twice as hard as the privileged guy...

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.600
...because you have to prove every single time...

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.360
...why you need to be in the team...

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.120
...even though you’re scoring more tries than anyone else

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.480
That’s why Chester believes that quotas are still needed...

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.080
...to ensure black players get into the national sport

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.520
If you don’t have the quota system then people won’t change...

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.840
...and players won’t come through the system

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.800
And in doing that we are seeing a lot of...

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.920
...black kids getting opportunities to play for the Springboks

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.600
Since the 1995 win...

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.880
...the Springboks team has incrementally become more balanced

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.720
And the Springboks selected more black and mixed-race players...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.160
...than ever before in 2018

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.920
But quotas not always popular

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.120
In a recent poll 82% of black South Africans...

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.720
...said that players should be picked solely on merit

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.800
And the perception that so-called quota players...

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.480
...don’t deserve to be selected is damaging

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.840
While I was playing I mean people would call me a quota player

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.840
It was almost like a smack in the face...

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.360
...that you’re not good enough to play there...

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.640
...but you’re selected only because of the colour of your skin

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:08.920
I can assure you we will carry 50m people in our hearts

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.360
As South Africa’s first black coach...

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.160
...Peter de Villiers’ appointment was mired in allegations...

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.920
...that it was politically motivated

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.400
They couldn’t handle that somebody of colour...

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.080
...would be at the helm of rugby

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.520
They never thought that it would happen

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.000
The last bastion of apartheid was rugby

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.640
So they tried to keep the game exclusive for them

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.160
He felt the significance of his appointment stretched far beyond sport

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.720
The overwhelming responsibility of getting this job...

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.320
...was born from the fact that we died in the street, you know

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.440
One of my friends was shot next to me during the apartheid years...

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.320
...when we were fighting for our freedom in the streets

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:02.680
And those things placed a huge, huge portion of pressure on my back

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.080
Unlike Chester, Peter believes that quotas are not the way to get...

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.880
...South Africa’s rugby team to better reflect the make-up of society

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.600
I don’t think quotas is your solution

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.720
What bothers me a lot about quotas at this moment is the fact...

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.200
...there’s no end period, no nothing

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.040
The most ambitious target yet has been set for 2019...

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:26.920
...that 50% of Springbok players...

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.720
...appearing over the course of the season are black...

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.000
...this includes the World Cup squad

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.880
When I was a coach I never looked at quotas, I never looked at race

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.200
The one thing that was very important for me—potential

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.800
One thing on which Chester and Peter both agree...

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.720
...is that the best way to nurture potential of black players...

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.160
...is to do so within their communities

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.400
I believe that we need to start it at a younger age...

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.560
...it should be done at school level and at provincial level...

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:58.360
...to make it easier for coaches to select those players

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:02.120
I would like to see that coming in the next ten years, maybe say...

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.920
...South Africa gets selected not because of the colour of their skin...

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.520
...but they get selected because they’re South Africans

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.240
They go now to these townships...

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.360
...find the best talent, remove them from that place...

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.080
...and put it in their schools

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.240
Wouldn’t it be better...

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.040
...if they upskilled those guys where they are?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.000
And at the level playing field you can see...

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.280
...who really is the best

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:32.560
Rugby’s struggle to transform is seen by some as...

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.400
...a metaphor for disillusionment among black people...

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.880
...who gained political, but not economic, freedom after apartheid

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.480
I am still surprised because...

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.120
...to see that people are still talking about quotas...

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.200
...because it’s 25 years since unification you know...

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.480
...and in sport we should have gone long past that

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:59.200
There was no repentance for apartheid

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.600
So those who tried to forgive, what did they forgive?

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:07.680
Who did they forgive?

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.120
So this conversation, for another 25 years, will still go on

